    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Fabric Dyeing\r\n\r\nUse `fabric_dye_log.csv` to practice filtering and aggregating data.\r\n\r\n::: details [✅ Step 1]\r\nCreate a filtered DataFrame containing dyes that:\r\n\r\n- Have an `Ingredient One` of `\"Indigo\"`\r\n- Have a non-null `Ingredient Two`\r\n\r\nUse AND (`&`) to combine the conditions. Print the first five rows.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [✅ Step 2]\r\nCreate a filtered DataFrame containing dyes whose `Color Result` ends with `\"k\"`. Print the first five rows.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [✅ Step 3]\r\nCreate a filtered DataFrame containing dyes that:\r\n\r\n- Have a `Fabric Type` of `\"Linen\"`\r\n- Have a `Time to Dye` greater than `100`\r\n- Have an `Ingredient Two` of either `\"Black Tea\"` or `\"Cutch\"`\r\n\r\nUse parentheses to group the two Ingredient Two conditions. Print the first five rows.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [✅ Step 4]\r\nGroup the data by `Color Result`. Calculate the count and median of `Time to Dye` for each color. Print the summary.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [Need Help?]\r\nUse AI Tutor to look up pandas documentation, explain your filter, or request a hint. When debugging a compound filter, check what each condition returns before combining the conditions.\r\n:::",
